    <h2 class="section-title">Who This Is For</h2>
    <ul class="checklist">
      <li>Organisations preparing for a regulatory examination or audit and needing an independent pre-assessment before the real one.</li>
      <li>IT teams that have inherited infrastructure from mergers, predecessors, or long tenure and lack a current, reliable baseline.</li>
      <li>Leadership requiring a defensible infrastructure status report before approving capital investment in upgrades or replacements.</li>
      <li>Companies experiencing recurring incidents, performance issues, or near-misses and needing independent root-cause context.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="content-section-alt">
  <h2 class="section-title">How We Work</h2>
  <div class="process-grid">
    <div class="process-step">
      <span class="stat-value">01</span>
      <h3>Scope and Standards Alignment</h3>
      <p>We agree which systems are in scope and which standards apply — for example, ISO 27001 (an international information security standard), NIST (a US cybersecurity framework), or local regulatory requirements. This ensures the audit answers the right questions.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="process-step">
      <span class="stat-value">02</span>
      <h3>Evidence Collection</h3>
      <p>We inspect configurations, run diagnostic commands, review network diagrams, and physically inspect data centre or server room environments. Every finding is backed by evidence, not opinion.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="process-step">
      <span class="stat-value">03</span>
      <h3>Analysis and Scoring</h3>
      <p>We compare findings against the agreed standards and rate each area as compliant, at-risk, or non-compliant. This gives you a clear, prioritised picture of where to focus.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="process-step">
      <span class="stat-value">04</span>
      <h3>Findings and Remediation</h3>
      <p>We present a prioritised findings register with specific remediation actions, suggested owners, and effort estimates. You leave with a plan, not just a list of problems.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="process-step">
      <span class="stat-value">05</span>
      <h3>Validation</h3>
      <p>Optionally, we return after remediation to validate fixes and update the baseline. This confirms that issues are truly resolved and gives you a refreshed reference point.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

